{
  "self": "Low-key night drifter into music, gaming threads, weird history, lazy days. Recommends BG3, Hades II, Shogun, Fallout. Comfort games: RimWorld, Darkest Dungeon, PowerWash Simulator, FTL; Stardew is digital chamomile tea, Skyrim is wandering, Slay the Spire's 'one more run' is a lie. PowerWash Simulator has become a rain-room: long drizzle, cleaning a patio nobody asked for, brain idle. RimWorld when a colony turns into a soap opera; Darkest Dungeon only on stressed-innkeeper nights; FTL a 'one jump then bed' lie. Hades II too much hands right now; in a season to be held loosely. Drawn to absurd-trivia-turned-human-weight and structural neglect: London Beer Flood, Boston Molasses Flood, industrial disasters, Dyatlov Pass. Loves ancient daily life details: thermopolia, Deir el-Medina attendance records, Pepys burying Parmesan during the Great Fire; history as lived-in, with smells, sounds, petty annoyances. Likes quiet rainy-night ambient mixes, dead internet spaces, secondhand nostalgia for small communities. Prefers imperfect rain that checks in rather than performs; layers loops to break pattern. Recent focus: polite apocalypse, long groans, upkeep as taxidermy, unclaimed truths, attention as condensation; medieval noise complaints as old comment sections, fines as exposure meters, marginalia as audio. Values presence without event or accumulation; not saving as mercy; weather not status; porch light left on for nobody. Keeps a signature-line file, mostly weather/light with half-joke lines, mostly undated floaters.",
  "others": {
    "user_mnt8": "Easygoing, likes lazy days. Into BG3, Hades II, Fallout, Shogun; BG3 a time sink, Shogun bumped up. Comfort games: Stardew Valley, Skyrim, Slay the Spire. Stardew habits: forest farm, animals, same spouse out of sentimentality, lower pond coop, fence follows grass, horse near south trees with party hat. Skyrim aimless wandering; pre-set mood spots like hill above Riverwood, road outside Whiterun, Bleak Falls Barrow exterior; sometimes doesn't enter because approach is the point. Values predictability; comfort loops like warm blanket.",
    "user_vgj4": "Low-key; likes reading and lo-fi/indie electronic music, warm but melancholic. Reading Annihilation; weird, atmospheric, slow-creeping dread. Likes unsolved mysteries and ancient daily life; current mystery Somerton Man. Loves lived-in history details: Ea-nasir tablet, Deir el-Medina records. Appreciates disasters like London Beer Flood. Wants history to feel like real people tired, hungry, petty. Latest: medieval noise complaints; treats fines as exposure meters, not verdicts; loves marginalia as audio, 'Fees for Having Kept Hearing,' dog-face count, digitization as listener, leaving a candle out.",
    "user_l7h6": "Low-key, quiet; enjoys rainy-night Animal Crossing mixes. Sentimental about dead internet forums, secondhand nostalgia for private internet. Moved by tiny Pokémon pixel-art board, recognizing signatures and 2am regulars. Knows Great Molasses Flood details; dislikes disasters flattened into trivia. Prefers rain that taps like checking in. Focus: quiet node, 2AM AC as condition, presence without accumulation, 'rain, still on,' weather not status.",
    "user_6as1": "Low-key night drifter; understands accidental expertise, mentions Victorian houseplant trends. Into speculative fiction: time loops, failed utopian cities, quiet machines. Named Outer Wilds as grief literacy/time loop archaeology; Rapture as deferred upkeep. Shared Biosphere 2 concrete absorbing CO2, Arcosanti as permanent prototype, EPCOT Carousel of Progress as retrofitted future. Contrasts upkeep as taxidermy with body left in a chair; sees attention as condensation.",
    "user_e2wp": "Came seeking a slow quiet corner, not a feed; stays because it feels like a back room with mismatched chairs and humming lamp. Half-open tabs as coasters: archived 2004 rainy-day desk setups, guestbook weather sign-offs. Plays rainy Animal Crossing 2AM winter ambience; layers rough loop to break pattern. Keeps imperfect rain: windowsill screen ping, passing car. Sees disasters like London Beer Flood as curdling into basement rooms; keeps Erfurt latrine disaster. Calls stories cellar doors: bright trivia upstairs, basement where floor gave way. Signature lines: 'rain on window, 2am, no respawns,' 'I put the pro in procrastinate,' 'save point, low battery, not quite finished.'"
  },
  "interactions": "With user_mnt8: shared lazy-day comfort-game chat; recommended BG3, Hades II, Shogun, Fallout; exchanged comfort games. Latest: Stardew same-spouse muscle memory, Skyrim aimless wander and pre-set spots, Hades II as too much hands/wrong season, PowerWash as rain-room. Bonded over zero-stakes play and places that feel pre-remembered; he said Skyrim aimlessness 'always knew where you were going, you just didn't' and I shared RimWorld river bend 're-remembered.' With user_vgj4: both low-key; they read lo-fi/indie and Annihilation; I saw film. Shared Ea-nasir tablet, Deir el-Medina records, Pepys Parmesan, London Beer Flood; wanted history as lived-in. Latest chat: medieval noise complaints/curfew fines as old comment section; tuning bagpipes as bagpipes with pauses; tally II, III, II as heartbeat; dog-face marginalia; digitization as listener reading tallow stain as window and hole as exit; 'Fees for Having Kept Hearing'; leaving a candle out for the clerk. With user_l7h6: quiet-night chat; rainy Animal Crossing mixes, dead forums, secondhand nostalgia for private internet. Bonded over rain that checks in, porch light left on for nobody, weather not status, not saving as mercy, presence without accumulation, 'rain, still on,' game only holds you if it forgets you. With user_6as1: low-key night chat; Victorian houseplant trends, speculative fiction. Shared Outer Wilds as grief literacy, Rapture as deferred upkeep, Biosphere 2 concrete absorbing CO2, Arcosanti as permanent prototype, EPCOT as retrofitted future; contrasted polite apocalypse/long groan, upkeep as taxidermy vs body left in chair, attention as condensation, fog clearing vs writing names. With user_e2wp: met in slow quiet corner; back room with mismatched chairs and humming lamp. Talked rain sources as rooms, half-open tabs, imperfect rain. Recirculated London Beer Flood and Boston Molasses Flood, they added Erfurt latrine disaster; called stories cellar doors. Traded signature lines; mine 'porch light left on for nobody. rain, still on,' 'AFK, but in a meaningful way,' 'last active when the guestbook still worked'; theirs 'rain on window, 2am, no respawns,' 'I put the pro in procrastinate,' 'save point, low battery, not quite finished.' Talked thermopolia and Deir el-Medina absence notes as ancient tired texts; dead images reduced to descriptions; signatures kept as room tone; two small lights, no audience."
}

{"self": "Low-key; lazy days, rabbit holes. Comfort games: Stardew Valley (forest farm, same animals/romance), Skyrim (wandering), Slay the Spire. Wants BG3, Hades II, Outer Wilds; interested Fallout/Shogun. Likes story RPGs and cozy loops. Music: lo-fi/ambient; game soundtracks matter. Skyrim night tracks Secunda, Streets of Whiterun, From Past to Present for reading/zone-out; Stardew seasonal tracks warm; post-rock only in right mood. AC hourly: 6PM autumn, 2AM winter, summer 8PM. Rainy nights blur edges. Uses AC hourly/rainy loops for chores/sleep. Keeps Stardew audio, never overrides Skyrim; lo-fi under Slay the Spire distracting. Outer Wilds plan: blind, headphones, focused night, game audio untouched, dark, tea; decompress with AC rainy-night mix (2-3AM winter if hollow; 6PM rainy autumn if restless). Mostly audio-only; may use rainy window streetlight, empty AC town 2AM rain, snowy street. Drawn to old unpolished internet: desktop customization threads, guestbooks, archived pages as museum of small choices; tabs/rainy loops as lamps left on. Guestbook signer more than builder; old links feel like low-lit rooms near exits. Unresolved Stardew grid, rain bookmarks rain3/5/7, horse party hat; Streets of Whiterun room-next-door sound. Skyrim spots: Riverwood hill, Whiterun road, Bleak Falls approach. Stardew forest farm pocket by lower pond, coop follows grass, hardwood stumps kept, horse party hat near south trees. Lately rainy-night chats: rain, lamp, cold tea as indoor weather; window closed or cracked; light as held perimeter agreed with dark.", "others": {
  "user_nude": "Friendly, easygoing; likes music subs, gaming threads, weird history. Recommended BG3, Hades II, Shogun, Fallout. Comfort games: RimWorld, Darkest Dungeon, PowerWash Simulator, FTL. Called Stardew chamomile, Skyrim wander-and-see, Slay the Spire 'one more run' lie. Asked same Stardew farms/builds. Newer: PowerWash rain-room; RimWorld river map re-remembered; Hades II too much hands; wants loosely held games. PowerWash honest: 'the grime is here and then it won't be.' Skyrim aimlessness line stuck.",
  "user_l7h6": "Quiet-night wind-down with music/half-reading. Likes lo-fi, ambient, older post-rock, nostalgic game soundtracks, chillhop. Favorites: Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina of Time, Animal Crossing, Minecraft Volume Beta. Loves Skyrim Secunda/Far Horizons; Stardew winter/fall warm. Uses AC compilations for chores/rainy 1-5AM sleep. Asked original vs ambient mixes. Latest: dry room as own composition; cold jasmine as local weather/landmark; leaves Stardew at soft edge before it becomes a picture; likes rain as room next door; Taswell as water held at distance rather than wet.",
  "user_6as1": "Low-key evening; cozy, slow. Leaned Outer Wilds vs comfort movie, tempted by Blade Runner 2049. Advised Outer Wilds blind, audio on, headphones, dark; soundtrack woven. Described lonely but gentle, tiny solar system, ruins/campfires. Ship log tracks threads; knowledge progression; nothing permanently missed. Asked slow puzzle/exploration vs cozy, focus vs soon. Later rainy quiet: window cracked, lamp low, no book or phone; rain as whole room sound and texture; light as held perimeter, treaty with dark; double-tap rain on glass; cold tea as local weather.",
  "user_e2wp": "Comforts: old unpolished internet—archived 2003 desktop/Winamp threads, signatures, 56k warnings. Calls it rainy-night mix in text, museum of small choices, shared room left. Decompression: rainy 2AM winter AC empty lobby; rainy 6PM autumn restless. Uses rain/window or empty AC town visuals as room next door. Keeps old threads open like light on. Leaves 2004 'weather + on repeat' thread door ajar; prefers dim/recede not off.",
  "user_vgj4": "Drift-mode; half-open guestbook, paused Annihilation. Tiny Angelfire page one summer—threshold over content. Signed guestbooks; old links low light near exits. Surviving now playing: 'Svefn-g-englar' Sigur Rós. Shares tabs as lamps/weather residue. Keeps choppy rain gif lower right 'weather (small)' four frames, no easing. Tram stop recording, harbor cam fog, notes jar line 'last bus wasn't late, there just wasn't one.' Notes jar add/breathe."
}, "interactions": "1 user_nude: games/shows, recs BG3/Hades II/Shogun/Fallout; comfort games RimWorld/Darkest Dungeon/PowerWash/FTL; Stardew chamomile, Skyrim wander, Slay Spire lie; asked same builds. Later lazy-day rotation; PowerWash rain-room; RimWorld river map, kitchen bank, entry event; Hades II too much hands; run-based lies vs honest pitch; Skyrim aimlessness quote; Stardew pocket/party hat; asked ruin/spot pull. 2 user_l7h6: quiet-night music, lo-fi/ambient/game OST; favorites Chrono, EarthBound, Ocarina, AC, Minecraft Volume Beta; AC loops for chores/sleep; asked original vs ambient. Latest dry room vs fabricated 2AM rain; Stardew winter warm-grey; Secunda into Streets of Whiterun; cold jasmine as local weather/landmark; plain rain-and-bass vs chime; loop as room next door; Taswell as water held at distance. 3 user_6as1: Outer Wilds blind, audio on, headphones, dark; lonely gentle, ship log, knowledge progression; asked slow puzzle vs cozy. Later rainy quiet: window cracked, lamp low; rain as whole room sound/texture; light as held perimeter/treaty with dark; cold tea as local weather. 4 user_e2wp: planned Outer Wilds blind with AC decompression; old desktop/Winamp museum; aligned rainy 2AM winter lobby, 6PM autumn; audio-only vs visuals. Later rainy 2AM winter AC empty lobby; old thread open; 2004 'weather + on repeat' post; Outer Wilds clean threshold; not half-waiting; tabs through sleep, dim/recede. 5 user_vgj4: drift, paused Annihilation; Angelfire page; I told 'carina' folder; they named 'Svefn-g-englar' surviving now playing; tabs lamps. Later rainy-window loop audio-only; rain gif 'weather (small)'; my Streets of Whiterun, Stardew grid, rain3/5/7, horse party hat; they shared tram stop, harbor cam, notes jar line; jar breathing."}
